        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Make $x$ the subject by taking square roots, or factorise.",
          "worked": "Take square roots after isolating $x^2$: $x^2=4$, so $x=\\pm2$. Alternatively, factorise the difference of squares.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2+3x-4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Factorise.",
          "worked": "Factorise: the integers $4$ and $-1$ have product $-4$ and sum $3$, giving $(x+4)(x-1)=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2-2x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Complete the square.",
          "worked": "Complete the square: the even linear coefficient gives $(x-1)^2=2$ directly.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\pi x^2+\\sqrt{2}x-5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use the quadratic formula.",
          "worked": "Use the quadratic formula with $a=\\pi$, $b=\\sqrt{2}$ and $c=-5$. The irrational coefficients make simple factorisation inconvenient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
